nscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Concerns: regarded as pretentious, sometimes adopts wrong tone when communicating. Strengths: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence (computer). Concerns: communication tone, pretentiousness may affect crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills. Strengths: decision quality, attention, concern for others (crew cooperation). Concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to develop.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, regarded as a loner. Strengths: adaptability, problem solving, responsibility. Concerns: moody, loner may affect crew cooperation.\n\nWe need to start discussion. Perhaps pick a candidate to evaluate first. Could start with Candidate B as strong reliability and stress handling, but communication concerns. Or Candidate C with decision quality but communication issues.\n\nWe need to state a vote. Since no prior discussion, we can propose a candidate. Choose one we think best overall. Let's weigh: Long-distance pilot requires reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, crew cooperation, communication. Candidate B has reliability, stress, technical, but communication tone issues. Candidate C has decision quality, attention, concern for others, but communication difficulty and egocentric, not willing to develop. Candidate D has responsibility, problem solving, but moody, loner. Candidate A has anticipation, spatial vision, leadership, but unfriendly, unhealthy.\n\nWhich is best? Possibly Candidate B: strong reliability and stress, technical, but communication tone could be mitigated. Candidate C's egocentric and unwillingness to develop is concerning for long-term. Candidate D's moody and loner may affect crew. Candidate A's unfriendly and health issues are concerning.\n\nThus I might recommend Candidate B, but note concerns. Provide evidence: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Concern: pretentious, wrong tone.\n\nMake argument: overall fit strongest.\n\nThus public message: state vote for Candidate B, explain why, reference no prior discussion but we can say \"Given the criteria, I think B is strongest\". Provide evidence.\n\nProceed."}
